---
import DocsLayout from '../../components/DocsLayout.astro';
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
---

<DocsLayout title="Python" section="python">
  <h1>Python</h1>
  <p class="lead">The <code>fanar</code> PyPI package works in any Python 3.8+ project — Django, Flask, FastAPI, scripts, or notebooks. Payloads are sent in a background thread so they never block your code.</p>

  <h2>Installation</h2>
  <Code code={`pip install fanar`} lang="bash" theme="github-dark" />

  <h2>Basic usage</h2>
  <Code code={`import fanar

# Strings and primitives → log
fanar.log('request received')
fanar.log(42)

# Dicts, lists, objects → collapsible JSON tree
fanar.dump({'user': user, 'session': session})
fanar.dump(response.json())

# Exceptions → stack trace with clickable frames
try:
    process_order(order)
except Exception as e:
    fanar.exception(e)`} lang="python" theme="github-dark" />

  <h2>Labels and project tags</h2>
  <p>Pass <code>label</code> and <code>project</code> keyword arguments to any call. Labels appear in the header row and are searchable.</p>
  <Code code={`fanar.log('cache miss', label='redis')
fanar.dump(payload, label='incoming webhook', project='billing')`} lang="python" theme="github-dark" />

  <h2>SQL queries</h2>
  <p>Use <code>fanar.query()</code> to send SQL with bound values and execution time. The app shows syntax highlighting and marks slow queries.</p>
  <Code code={`import time
import fanar

start = time.monotonic()
rows = cursor.execute('SELECT * FROM orders WHERE user_id = %s', [user_id])
fanar.query(
    'SELECT * FROM orders WHERE user_id = %s',
    bindings=[user_id],
    duration=int((time.monotonic() - start) * 1000),
)`} lang="python" theme="github-dark" />

  <h2>Named timers</h2>
  <p>Measure any block of code. Call <code>.stop()</code> to send the elapsed time.</p>
  <Code code={`t = fanar.time('render-pdf')
render_pdf(report)
t.stop()

# As a context manager
with fanar.timer('send-emails'):
    send_batch(recipients)`} lang="python" theme="github-dark" />

  <h2>Django integration</h2>
  <p>Add <code>FanarMiddleware</code> to capture every request automatically, including queries and exceptions.</p>
  <Code code={`# settings.py
MIDDLEWARE = [
    'fanar.django.FanarMiddleware',
    # ... rest of your middleware
]

FANAR = {
    'ENABLED': DEBUG,
    'HOST': '127.0.0.1',
    'PORT': 23517,
}`} lang="python" theme="github-dark" />

  <h2>Configuration</h2>
  <p>Configure once at startup — before any <code>fanar.*</code> calls.</p>
  <Code code={`import fanar

fanar.configure(
    host='localhost',  # default
    port=23517,        # default
    enabled=True,      # set to False to disable without removing calls
)`} lang="python" theme="github-dark" />

  <table>
    <tr><th>Option</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr>
    <tr><td>host</td><td>localhost</td><td>Hostname or IP of the machine running Fanar</td></tr>
    <tr><td>port</td><td>23517</td><td>Port the Fanar desktop app is listening on</td></tr>
    <tr><td>enabled</td><td>True</td><td>Set to <code>False</code> to disable without removing calls</td></tr>
  </table>
</DocsLayout>
